From 1240a1c2c6894820c49f8326f458c021653b9f5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 15:57:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] iommu/vsi: check that the DMA mask was applied

vsi_iommu_probe() discards the dma_set_mask_and_coherent() return
value. The IOMMU walks a page table it addresses with 32-bit hardware
registers, so a platform that cannot apply the mask must fail the probe
rather than continue with a wider one.

Fixes: 917ace84b770 ("iommu: Add verisilicon IOMMU driver")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c
index 8193fd62161fd..808e52bf9efc3 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c
@@ -703,7 +703,10 @@ static int vsi_iommu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (err)
 		goto err_unprepare_clocks;
 
-	dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	err = dma_set_mask_and_coherent(dev, DMA_BIT_MASK(32));
+	if (err)
+		goto err_unprepare_clocks;
+
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, iommu);
 
 	pm_runtime_set_autosuspend_delay(dev, 100);
-- 
